            0.364,
            0.063
          ],
          "content": [
            {
              "type": "text",
              "content": "Ganita Prakash | Grade 7"
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "index": 1,
          "bbox": [
            0.149,
            0.088,
            0.848,
            0.146
          ],
          "content": [
            {
              "type": "text",
              "content": "Even in this case, the area of rectangle AEFD can be found in two ways: (i) by directly using the side lengths n and (12 – 4), or (ii) subtracting the area of the rectangle EBCF from that of ABCD."
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "type": "chart",
          "index": 2,
          "bbox": [
            0.241,
            0.162,
            0.757,
            0.347
          ],
          "content": [
            {
              "type": "chart_body",
              "index": 2,
              "bbox": [
                0.241,
                0.162,
                0.757,
                0.347
              ],
              "image_path": "images/page_9_chart_2.jpg",
              "content": ""
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "index": 3,
          "bbox": [
            0.15,
            0.363,
            0.848,
            0.419
          ],
          "content": [
            {
              "type": "text",
              "content": "The first method gives us 8n, and the second method gives us "
            },
            {
              "type": "equation_inline",
              "content": "1 2 n - 4 n"
            },
            {
              "type": "text",
              "content": " , and they are equal, since "
            },
            {
              "type": "equation_inline",
              "content": "12n - 4n = 8n"
            },
            {
              "type": "text",
              "content": " . This is the expression for the area of the rectangle AEFD."
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "index": 4,
          "bbox": [
            0.149,
            0.419,
            0.847,
            0.474
          ],
          "content": [
            {
              "type": "text",
              "content": "Sets of terms such as (5c, c, 10c), "
            },
            {
              "type": "equation_inline",
              "content": "(12n, -4n)"
            },
            {
              "type": "text",
              "content": " that involve the same letter-numbers are called "
            },
            {
              "type": "text",
              "content": "like terms",
              "styles": [
                "bold"
              ]
            },
            {
              "type": "text",
              "content": ". Sets of terms such as {18c, 11d} are called "
            },
            {
              "type": "text",
              "content": "unlike terms",
              "styles": [
                "bold"
              ]
            },
            {
              "type": "text",
              "content": " as they have different letter-numbers."
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "index": 5,
          "bbox": [
            0.149,
            0.475,
            0.846,
            0.512
          ],
          "content": [
            {
              "type": "text",
              "content": "As we have seen, like terms can be added together and simplified into a single term."
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "index": 6,
          "bbox": [
            0.111,
            0.52,
            0.532,
            0.598
          ],
          "content": [
            {
              "type": "text",
              "content": "Example 7:",
              "styles": [
                "bold"
              ]
            },
            {
              "type": "text",
              "content": " A shop rents out chairs and tables for a day’s use. To rent them, one has to first pay the following amount per piece."
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "type": "table",
          "index": 7,
          "bbox": [
            0.542,
            0.51,
            0.843,
            0.592
          ],
          "content": [
            {
              "type": "table_body",
              "index": 7,
              "bbox": [
                0.542,
                0.51,
                0.843,
                0.592
              ],
              "image_path": "images/page_9_table_7.jpg",
              "content": "<table><tbody><tr><td>Item</td><td>Amount</td></tr><tr><td>Chair</td><td>₹40</td></tr><tr><td>Table</td><td>₹75</td></tr></tbody></table>"
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "index": 8,
          "bbox": [
            0.15,
            0.601,
            0.525,
            0.656
          ],
          "content": [
            {
              "type": "text",
              "content": "When the furniture is returned, the shopkeeper pays back some amount as follows."
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "index": 9,
          "bbox": [
            0.148,
            0.657,
            0.525,
            0.712
          ],
          "content": [
            {
              "type": "text",
              "content": "Write an expression for the total number of rupees paid if x chairs and y tables are rented."
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "type": "table",
          "index": 10,
          "bbox": [
            0.543,
            0.601,
            0.845,
            0.702
          ],
          "content": [
            {
              "type": "table_body",
              "index": 10,
              "bbox": [
                0.543,
                0.601,
                0.845,
                0.702
              ],
              "image_path": "images/page_9_table_10.jpg",
              "content": "<table><tbody><tr><td></td><td>Amount returned</td></tr><tr><td>Chair</td><td>₹6</td></tr><tr><td>Table</td><td>₹10</td></tr></tbody></table>"
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "index": 11,
          "bbox": [
            0.149,
            0.712,
            0.847,
            0.751
          ],
          "content": [
            {
              "type": "text",
              "content": "For x chairs and y tables, let us find the total amount paid at the beginning and the amount one gets back after returning the furniture."
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "index": 12,
          "bbox": [
            0.111,
            0.758,
            0.602,
            0.781
          ],
          "content": [
            {
              "type": "text",
              "content": "Describe the procedure to get these amounts."
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "index": 13,
          "bbox": [
            0.15,
            0.789,
            0.846,
            0.827
          ],
          "content": [
            {
              "type": "text",
              "content": "The total amount in rupees paid at the beginning is "
            },
            {
              "type": "equation_inline",
              "content": "4 0 x \\pm 7 5 y"
            },
            {
              "type": "text",
              "content": " , and the total amount returned is "
            },
            {
              "type": "equation_inline",
              "content": "6 x + 1 0 y ."
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "index": 14,
          "bbox": [
            0.174,
            0.827,
            0.676,
            0.847
          ],
          "content": [
            {
              "type": "text",
              "content": "So, the total amount pai "
            },
            {
              "type": "equation_inline",
              "content": "\\mathbf{d} = (40x + 75y) - (6x + 10y)."
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "index": 15,
          "bbox": [
            0.111,
            0.854,
            0.761,
            0.878
          ],
          "content": [
            {
              "type": "text",
              "content": "? Can we simplify this expression? If yes, how? If not, why not?"
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "type": "footer",
          "index": 16,
          "bbox": [
            0.818,
            0.838,
            0.905,
